\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\i\f0\fs22 Waste Management Recycling Education Representative Bobby Bell expressed appreciation to Interim Public Works Director Ted Semaan for his leadership and stated it was a pleasure working with him. He also thanked Skechers and the Chamber of Commerce for hosting a successful Holiday Fireworks Festival on Sunday, December 14, 2025. Additionally, he announced that due to the Christmas holiday, there will be no collection service on Thursday, December 25, 2025, and service will be delayed by one day for Thursday, Friday and Saturday collection days. The same schedule adjustment will apply for the New Year\rquote s holiday.\cf1\b\i0\line\line\cf0\b0\i Library Manager Cassandra Sargent announced a holiday sing-along scheduled for Saturday, December 20, 2025, at 2:00 PM. She also shared that teen study halls will be held on Wednesday, December 17, 2025, and Thursday, December 18, 2025, to support students preparing for finals. Additionally, she reported that new adult furniture has been installed, and children\rquote s furniture will be added in early spring of next year.\cf1\b\i0\line\line\cf0\b0\i Manhattan Beach resident Mike Jenkins announced that Manhattan Beach United, in collaboration with the Mira Costa High School Black Scholars Union, Pacific Islanders Club, Latino Scholars Union, St. Michael\rquote s Club, Middle Eastern North African (MENA) Club, Mira Costa Jazz Band, and Mira Costa Choir, will host a multicultural celebration at the Joslyn Community Center on February 22, 2026, from 2:00 to 4:00 PM.\cf1\b\i0\line\line\cf0\b0\i Councilmember Howorth extended holiday greetings, wishing those who celebrate a Happy Hanukkah and noting that the menorah lighting will take place on Thursday, December 18, 2025, at Metlox Plaza. She also wished everyone who celebrates a Merry Christmas and encouraged the community to gather with loved ones and bring light to the world.\cf1\b\i0\line\line\cf0\b0\i Councilmember Charelian announced that Manhattan Beach Little League registration has been extended and will close on December 30, 2025. Registration is available on the Manhattan Beach Little League website.\cf1\b\i0\line\line\cf0\b0\i Mayor Pro Tem Franklin announced that the Delancy Christmas Tree Lot has relocated to the Manhattan Village Mall parking lot. He also recognized Alessandra Stone and her co-workers for organizing a beach trash cleanup.\cf1\b\i0\line\line\pard\cf0\b0\i Mayor Lesser thanked and congratulated City staff and Skechers for organizing the Holiday Fireworks Festival last weekend. He invited the community to attend Coffee with the Mayor at Metlox Plaza on Friday, January 2, 2026, from 9:00 AM to 10:00 AM. He also announced that, as Mayor, he has signed a letter of condolence to the residents of Bondi Beach, Sydney, following the recent tragedy, and reaffirmed the City\rquote s commitment to combating anti-Semitism.\cf2\i0\f1\par
}


